*************************************************************************                     The Print Manager *                 	 Printer Port Driver** Coding Started Summer 1986 by Luc Barthelet and VersionSoft** Version 1.1d1    May 9, 1988       Suki Lee**	Added capability to read data from the printer, so we can get the ID from it.*   In DevOpen, added calls to set the printer as input device as well. In DevRead,*   added wait and status mechanisms, and changed call from ReadBlock to ReadLine.* ** Version 1.2** June 30, 1988         Suki Lee*    Changed macro _WriteBlock to its new name: _TextWriteBlock. *    Eliminated need to use Special.Macros.** August 2, 1988        Suki Lee*    Bug Fix:*    - In system disk 4.0, the ID string from the LQ arrives sooner than the firm-*      ware is ready to read it (due to interrupts). I/O buffering will have to be*      enabled right after initialization rather than just before a read. Moved the*      buffer enable code from DevRead to DevOpen. Also took out call to GetModeBits*      to check if buffering is already on since it doesn't hurt to have it on.* * August 12, 1988*    Bug FIx:*    - Carry was not set correctly after DevWrite, causing problems in the ImageWriter*      driver when printing in draft mode.** v2.0* d1 October 10, 1988    Suki Lee*    Fixed DevStartUp to remove two pointers off the stack since the same call in*    the AppleTalk driver uses two pointers as input.** d2 December 5, 1988    Suki Lee*    The new ROM allows slot 1 and 2 to be selectable among 3 options: Printer *    (or Modem), AppleTalk, or Your Card. The present code checks the slot state*    to determine if the slot is internal or external. This will not work for new*    ROMs since AppleTalk is considered internal. The code is modified to check*    ROM version number and check the appropriate location to determine if the slot*    is configured correctly.** d3 December 16, 1988    Suki Lee*    Added new header to denote this as a driver which will support new calls.*    This header is 2 words long: first word is 0 followed by a call count word.** d4 January 6, 1989      Suki Lee*     Buffering in the firmware is enabled so we can read the self ID response from *     the printer. There is problem with handshaking with the printer if the buffer*     is turned off so we left it on. AppleWorks GS ran into a problem where the *     reset for the next page happens before last part of the page is finished, *     losing the remaining data. Mike Askins suggests adding code to query the output  *     queue to make sure it is empty before the next firmware reset. Also added a *     flag to skip the query if the firmware has not been initialized.** d5 January 18, 1989     Suki Lee*    Removed DevInitBack since none of the code is used. Replaced it with DevAsyncRead*    with the corrected number of parameters, 4 instead of 3. Renamed DevFillBack to*    DevWriteBack and corrected the number of parameters from 2 to 3. Both these calls*    currently do nothing and are not used by the printer drivers.**    January 25, 1989     Suki Lee*    Added code to reset firmware after printing so the firmware's buffers will be *    deallocated. Also added code to remember and reset the output redirection back *    to the way we found it.*    *    May 25, 1989         Suki Lee*    Moved the code which queries the output buffer from DevOpen to DevClose, just *    before the firmware init call. The firmware was being initialized before the  *    buffer is cleared causing the system to hang in DevOpen for the next job, waiting *    for a buffer which has been deallocated to clear.**    August 22, 1989      Ben Koning*    Added a zap ("Ignore all subsequent ^I commands") command to DevOpen, so that*    ^I's ($09 or $89) in the data stream won't be interpreted and filtered out by*    the firmware.  Removed similar zap code from DevRead.*** v2.1 for System Disk 5.0.3**    NOTE: Several of the changes for v2.1 are really kludges and are implemented with the*    understanding that they will go away when a new PRINTER/MODEM port driver is written*    which uses a new GS/OS fast serial device driver.** d1 December 19, 1989      Suki Lee*    Modified the stack offset for DevAsyncRead to not include dpage and bank address*    since the call never switches dpage.** d2 January 2, 1990        Ben Koning*    Removed usage of PushPtr macro.** d3 May 3, 1990			Ben Koning*    If the Battery-RAM parameters indicate 19.2K baud with all other default settings, we*    bypass the texttool/serial-firmware and communicate with the SCC chip directly in the*    DevWrite call only.  This allows true 19.2K baud output until a better SCC driver*    is written.  2X perfomance gain; important for high resolution printers such as LQ, which*    becomes about 72% faster.** d4 May 25, 1990			Ben Koning*    If the current client-printer driver is version 4.0 or greater (as found by doing a*    PrGetDrvrVer call), then the timeout delay for the read call is much less.  This is*    because the old drivers requested a self-ID from the printer right after giving a*    time-consuming head recalibration command, and the printer does not respond during*    this time.  A shorter timeout delay is necessary in cases of the IW-I being connected*    (it doesn't reply to self-ID query) or if the cable was left unconnected or if the*    select light on the printer is off.  This needs to be tested for backward compatibility*    with the old IW driver and with both the ImageWriterII and the ImageWriterI.** d5 June 4, 1990			Ben Koning*    In the 19.2K baud handling code, the DCD and DSR handshake lines weren't being checked.***********************************************************************************************************************************************	Printer Port Driver Version 2.X*   Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1986-1989*	All rights reserved.***********************************************************************;------------------------------------------;; Equates from procedure ;;------------------------------------------VersionNb      equ $0201               ; Version 2.1NoError        equ 0                   ; No errorPortNotOn      equ $1302               ; Port not activeTrue           equ $FFFFFalse          equ $0000 ;-----------------------------------------------;;   Imported addresses;;-----------------------------------------------	IMPORT	alerttemp320	IMPORT	alerttemp640;-----------------------------------------------;;   Forward addresses and entries;;-----------------------------------------------	ENTRY	CallCompletion	ENTRY	Completion	ENTRY	DevClose	ENTRY	DevWriteBack	ENTRY	DevAsyncRead	ENTRY	DevIsItSafe	ENTRY	DevOpen	ENTRY	DevPrChanged	ENTRY	DevRead	ENTRY	DevShutDown	ENTRY	DevStartup	ENTRY	DevStatus	ENTRY	DevWrite	ENTRY	Exit10	ENTRY	Exit4	ENTRY	Exit6	ENTRY	Exit8	ENTRY	IsItSafe	ENTRY	PortAlert	ENTRY	PrPortVer	ENTRY	exit0	******************************                           ** ...The Printer Manager... **  Driver for Printer Port  **                           *******************************               Absaddr on*               Keep   Printer		include 'all.macros' 		EXPORT	Printerport   Printerport   PROC;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Header to denote new calls supported;	DC.W 0						; marker	DC.W (EndProcList-ProcList)/4 ; count of calls supported               jmp (ProcList,x)               rtl		EXPORT	ProcListProcList	DC.L	DevPrChanged			DC.L	DevStartup			DC.L	DevShutDown			DC.L	DevOpen			DC.L	DevRead			DC.L	DevWrite			DC.L	DevClose			DC.L	DevStatus			DC.L	DevAsyncRead			DC.L	DevWriteBack			DC.L	PrPortVer			DC.L	DevIsItSafe	; new call added 16 apr 87EndProcList 		ENDP;                Copy Device************************************************************** PrPortVer ** Returns version # of currently installed port*************************************************************		EXPORT	PrPortVer      PrPortVer      PROC               DefineStack Rtl1           Block 3Rtl2           Block 3Version        Word 0                lda #VersionNb               sta Version,s               lda #0                jmp exit0 		ENDP***************************************************************** DevPrChanged* * Called by Printer driver when it has been changed.  Gives* us change to tell user there may be a problem.* ***************************************************************		EXPORT	DevPrChanged   DevPrChanged   PROC               jsr IsItSafe               bcc Safe               pha               jsr PortAlert            ; put up alert               pla Safe           jmp Exit4		ENDP***************************************************************** DevStartup**        LONG	pointer to printer name*        LONG	pointer to zone name** call does nothing for serial ports* ***************************************************************		EXPORT	DevStartup     DevStartup     PROC               jsr IsItSafe               jmp Exit8		ENDP***************************************************************** DevShutDown** Does even less than startup since it takes no inputs.* ***************************************************************		EXPORT	DevShutDown    DevShutDown    PROC               jsr IsItSafe                jmp Exit0		ENDP***************************************************************** DevOpen**     OpenCompletion   LONG*     Reserved         LONG* ***************************************************************		EXPORT	DevOpen        DevOpen        PROC               DefineStack DevOpen_DPage  word 0DevOpen_BReg   byte 0DevOpen_rtl1   block 3DevOpen_rtl2   block 3Reserved       long 0OpenCompletion long 0               jsr IsItSafe               bcc OpenSafe               jmp Exit8		EXPORT	OpenSafeOpenSafe	;                phd               phb               phk                      plb               lda OpenCompletion,s               sta Completion               lda OpenCompletion+2,s               sta Completion+2			   ;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Find out what printer driver is requesting our services.  If v4.0 or greater, then; setup for shorter read-call timeout delay.;               stz IsNewPrDrvrFlag               pha			   _PrDriverVer			   pla			   cmp #$0400			   bcc isnewpr_no			   lda #1			   sta IsNewPrDrvrFlagisnewpr_no;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Need to save all old settings for input and output device for restoring later; in DevClose.;				lda #0				pha					; word space				pha				pha					; long space				_GetInputDevice				pla				sta InputSlot				pla					; high word				sta InputSlot+2				pla				sta InputType								lda #0				pha					; two word spaces				pha				_GetInGlobals				pla				sta InOrMask				pla				sta InAndMask								lda #0				pha					; word space				pha				pha					; long space				_GetOutputDevice				pla				sta OutputSlot				pla					; high word				sta OutputSlot+2				pla				sta OutputType								lda #0				pha					; two word spaces				pha				_GetOutGlobals				pla				sta OutOrMask				pla				sta OutAndMask				;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Set it up for our use now;               PushWord #1			; Pascal device type               PushLong #1			; slot number               _setInputDevice               PushWord #$ffff               PushWord #0               _setInGlobals               PushWord #0               _inittextDev			                  PushWord #1			; Pascal device type               PushLong #1			; slot number               _setOutputDevice               PushWord #$ffff               PushWord #0               _setoutGlobals               PushWord #1               _inittextDev			                  pushlong #InitGraph+1               pushword #0               lda InitGraph               and #$00ff               pha               _TextWriteBlock;-----------------------------------------------------------;; We need to enable the buffering for input characters via the firmware.; Experience has shown that if the input buffering is disabled, we can ; only get two characters from the ReadLine call. ;			   			   pushlong #BuffEnable			; turn I/O buffering on			   _WriteString			   ;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Make sure that no characters are interpreted by the firmware; as commands (ie, send all data RAW).;			   pushlong #Zap					; ignore all subsequent ^I commands			   _WriteString			   ;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Check to see if the Battery-RAM settings for slot 1 imply 19.2K baud; with all other default options.  If so, then set flag to allow direct; SCC communication/firware bypass kludge for greater speed.;NKBaudQualify				stz NKBaudEnableFlag			;clear enable flag; assume not defaults/19.2KB				ldy #0							;prepare to loop to check BRAM against our tableNKBaudQualLoop	phy								;save Y = index into tables				lda NKBaudBattRAMLocs,y			;find out a BRAM parameter that we should check				pha								;result space				pha								;pass BRAM param no.				_ReadBParam				pla								;obtain BRAM value				ply								;restore Y = index into tables				cmp NKBaudBattRAMVals,y			;compare BRAM value against table				bne NKBaudQualDone				;break off the search as soon as one doesn't match				iny								;else continue checking				iny				cpy #NKBaudBattRAMLen				bne NKBaudQualLoop				lda #1							;all BRAM params are as we want, so set enable flag				sta NKBaudEnableFlag				NKBaudQualDone			;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Call user's completion routine, if any, and exit.			   			                  jsl CallCompletion               plb               pld               jmp Exit8		EXPORT	CallCompletionCallCompletion		;		               lda Completion               ora Completion+2               bne doit               Rtl		EXPORT	DoitDoit	;                lda Completion+1               pha               phb               pla               lda Completion               sec               sbc #1               pha               rtl		EXPORT	CompletionCompletion		;				DS.B 4			EXPORT	InitGraphInitGraph	DC.B	14			DC.B	09,67,68			; disable line formating, (CD)			DC.B	09,84				; disable basic tab (T)			DC.B	09,70,68			; disable keyboard input (FD)			DC.B	09,77,68			; disable filtering LF (MD)			DC.B	09,76,68			; disable LF after CF (LD)BuffEnable	DC.B 3		; length			DC.B $09	; Control-I			DC.B 'BE'	; Enable bufferZap			DC.B 2			DC.B $09			DC.B 'Z'	;  zap						export IsNewPrDrvrFlagIsNewPrDrvrFlag			dc.w	0NKBaudBattRAMLen		equ		2*11NKBaudBattRAMLocs		dc.w	$08,$06,$01,$07,$02,$03,$05,$04,$09,$0A,$0BNKBaudBattRAMVals		dc.w	2,14,0,6,0,1,0,0,1,1,0						export	NKBaudEnableFlagNKBaudEnableFlag		dc.w	0			EXPORT InputSlotInputSlot	DS.B 4			EXPORT InputTypeInputType	DS.B 2			EXPORT InOrMaskInOrMask	DS.B 2			EXPORT InAndMaskInAndMask	DS.B 2			EXPORT OutputSlotOutputSlot	DS.B 4			EXPORT OutputTypeOutputType	DS.B 2			EXPORT OutOrMaskOutOrMask	DS.B 2			EXPORT OutAndMaskOutAndMask	DS.B 2			ENDP***************************************************************** DevRead**    Input*       PtrToBuffer   LONG*       MaxToXfer     WORD**    Output*       XferCount     WORD****************************************************************		EXPORT	DevRead        DevRead        PROC               DefineStackDevRead_DPage  word 0DevRead_BReg   byte 0DevRead_rtl1   block 3DevRead_rtl2   block 3ReadRqd        word 0    10PtrReadBuf     long 0    12readTrnsfrd    word 0    16               jsr IsItSafe               bcc ReadSafe               jmp Exit6 ReadSafe	;               phd               phb               phk               plb			   lda PtrReadBuf+2,s			   sta readBuf+2			   lda PtrReadBuf,s			   sta readBUf			   lda ReadRqd,s			   sta requestCount;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Aug 2, 1988 Suki Lee; Moved buffer enable code to DevOpen. Also removed extended interface call ; to firmware to check if buffer is enabled;;-----------------------------------------------------------;; This read routine has a timeout delay.  In the old printer drivers (<4.0),; the status-query read is done right after the given command to perform; head recalibration.;; The ImageWriter II will not respond while the print head is moving. ; Since we always reset the printer for each print job, it means that; the head is always moving.  The only difference is the distance it has; to travel to the left edge.  This counter value will work for the worst; case of when the printer was at the right edge when it was reset.  The; wait is noticable on ImageWriter I's since it has to wait out the whole; count.;; The above will now happen only if the current printer driver version is; less than 4.0; otherwise, a much shorter timeout value is used.;			   			   lda #$FFFF				; wait loop counter = $FFFF if old printer driver (~45 s)			   import IsNewPrDrvrFlag			   ldx IsNewPrDrvrFlag			   beq setup_counter			   lda #$0B00				; wait loop counter is less if new printer driver (~2 s)setup_counter  sta counter			   LoopStatus			   lda #0			   pha			   pha			   pha			   pha						; result spaces			   inc a					; A reg: input request = 1			   pha									   lda #$00C1				; X reg			   pha			   lda #$0010				; Y reg			   pha			   lda >$00C110				; status offset			   clc			   adc #$C100				; entry point			   pha			   _FWEntry			   pla			   pla			   pla			   pla						; get processor status			   xba						; only high byte is valid			   and #$0001				; check the carry bit			   bne TimeToRead			; 0 means not ready yet			   lda counter			   dec a			   beq Exit			   sta counter			   bra loopStatusTimeToRead	   pha						; result: actual read count			   PushLong readBuf			   lda requestCount			; amount to be read			   pha			   lda #$0D					; EOL char = carriage return			   pha			   lda #0			   pha						; don't echo			   _ReadLine			   plaExit		   sta ReadTrnsfrd,s			   ;-----------------------------------------------------------;; The following two line of code were taken out because it cause some; problem with handshaking between the firmware and the printer. Mike ; Askins is unsure of the exact cause at this point and this code is; left here so a test case can be recreated for him;			   ;			   pushlong #BuffDisable		; we did, so we turn it back off;			   _WriteString			   plb               pld               jmp Exit6readBuf			DS.B 4requestCount	DS.B 2counter			DS.B 2		ENDP						***************************************************************** DevWrite**      WriteCompletion   LONG*      SrcBufPtr         LONG*      Length            WORD* ***************************************************************		EXPORT	DevWrite       DevWrite       PROC               DefineStackDevWrite_DPage word 0DevWrite_BReg  byte 0DevWrite_rtl1  block 3DevWrite_rtl2  block 3WriteLengths   word 0WritePtrBuff   long 0WriteCompletion long 0                jsr IsItSafe                bcc WriteSafe                brl Exit10 WriteSafe                phd							;save D, save B, do B=K                phb                phk                plb                lda WriteCompletion,s		;setup so we can call user's completion routine                sta Completion+0                lda WriteCompletion+2,s                sta Completion+2			   				import NKBaudEnableFlag		;check to see if default/19.2KBaud is selected				lda NKBaudEnableFlag		;if so then do our fast shortcut kludge				beq WriteNKBNo				;otherwise write the data through the firmwareWriteNKBYes				lda WritePtrBuff+0,s		;writing the data out directly to the SCC chip...				sta WriteNKBGetData+1		;set up stuffed operands				lda WritePtrBuff+2,s				shortm				sta WriteNKBGetData+3				longm				lda WriteLengths,s				sta WriteNKBCmpLen+1				ldx #0						;init counter into user's data, set 8-bit mode				shortmWriteNKBLoop	lda >$E0C039				;poll SCC ch. A command register bit to see if ready				tay				bit #%00000100				;check: b5)DSR, b3)DCD, b2)TxBuffer ready				beq WriteNKBLoop				tya				bit #%00100000				beq WriteNKBLoop				tya				bit #%00001000				beq WriteNKBLoop			WriteNKBGetData	lda >$FFFFFF,x				;NOTE: operand is stuffed.  get a byte from user				sta >$E0C03B				;write into SCC ch. A data register				inx							;advance our pointer into user's dataWriteNKBCmpLen	cpx #$FFFF					;NOTE: operand is stuffed				bcc WriteNKBLoop				longm						;reset to 16-bit mode when done								jsl CallCompletion			;call user's routine, restore B/D, exit no error				lda #0				plb				pld				brl Exit10				WriteNKBNo			                   lda WritePtrBuff+2,s		;writing the data out through the serial firmware...                pha                lda WritePtrBuff+2,s                pha                lda WriteLengths+4,s                tax                lda #0                pha                phx                _TextWriteBlock				;text tool call, calls serial firmware							    pha							;exiting: save error                jsl CallCompletion			;call user's routine			    pla 						;restore error in A                plb							;restore B, restore D, and exit                pld                brl Exit10								ENDP***************************************************************** DevClose** no parameters****************************************************************		EXPORT	DevClose       DevClose       PROC               jsr IsItSafe			   bcc CloseSafe               Jmp Exit0CloseSafe                     phd               phb               phk               plb			   php			   			   sei				; disable interrupts			   				lda #0				pha				pha				pha				pha					; result spaces				lda #GetModeBitsParam				tax					and #$00FF			; A reg: low byte of address of parameters				pha								txa 				; X reg: mid byte of address				xba				and #$00FF				pha				lda #^GetModeBitsParam ; Y reg: high byte of address				and #$00FF				pha				lda >$00C112		; extended interface offset				clc				adc #$C100			; entry point				pha				_FWEntry				pla				pla				pla				pla					lda GetModeBits				sta SetModeBits				lda GetModeBits+2				and #$FF7F			; clear the zap bit -- turn on ^I command interpret				sta SetModeBits+2					lda #0				pha				pha				pha				pha					; result spaces				lda #SetModeBitsParam				tax					and #$00FF			; A reg: low byte of address of parameters				pha								txa 				; X reg: mid byte of address				xba				and #$00FF				pha				lda #^SetModeBitsParam ; Y reg: high byte of address				and #$00FF				pha				lda >$00C112		; extended interface offset				clc				adc #$C100			; entry point				pha				_FWEntry				pla				pla				pla				pla									plp				; reenable interrupt								lda #0				pha				pha				pha				pha					; result spaces				lda #GetOutBufferParam				tax					and #$00FF			; A reg: low byte of address of parameters				pha								txa 				; X reg: mid byte of address				xba				and #$00FF				pha				lda #^GetOutBufferParam ; Y reg: high byte of address				and #$00FF				pha				lda >$00C112		; extended interface offset				clc				adc #$C100			; entry point				pha				_FWEntry				pla				pla				pla				pla					loopQuery		lda #0				pha				pha				pha				pha					; result spaces				lda #OutQStatusParam				tax					and #$00FF			; A reg: low byte of address of parameters				pha								txa 				; X reg: mid byte of address				xba				and #$00FF				pha				lda #^OutQStatusParam ; Y reg: high byte of address				and #$00FF				pha				lda >$00C112		; extended interface offset				clc				adc #$C100			; entry point				pha				_FWEntry				pla				pla				pla				pla									lda BufferLeng		; capacity found with GetOutBuffer call				dec a							cmp SpaceLeft		; free space found with OutQStatus call				bne loopQuery		; if they are equal, then nothing is left in buffer				;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Reset the firmware so the buffer will be disposed of;			   pushlong #ResetFW			   _WriteString			   			   ;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Reset the input and output devices to whatever it was before we changed it.;			   PushWord InputType	; Pascal device type               PushLong InputSlot	; slot number               _setInputDevice               PushWord InAndMask               PushWord InOrMask               _setInGlobals               PushWord #0               _inittextDev			                  PushWord OutputType	; Pascal device type               PushLong OutputSlot	; slot number               _setOutputDevice               PushWord OutAndMask               PushWord OutOrMask               _setoutGlobals               PushWord #1               _inittextDev			                   plb               pld               jmp Exit0			   GetModeBitsParam				DC.B $03		; parameter count			DC.B $00		; command code for GetModeBits			DS.B 2			; result codeGetModeBits	DS.B 4			; Mode bits			SetModeBitsParam				DC.B $03		; parameter count			DC.B $01		; command code for SetModeBits			DS.B 2			; result codeSetModeBits	DS.B 4			; Mode bits			GetOutBufferParam				DC.B $04	; parameter count			DC.B $11	; command code for GetOutBuffer			DS.B 2		; result code			DS.B 4		; buffer addressBufferLeng	DS.B 2		; buffer length			OutQStatusParam				DC.B $04	; parameter count			DC.B $17	; command code for OutQStatus			DS.B 2		; result codeSpaceLeft	DS.B 2		; space left in output queue			DS.B 2		; reserved							ResetFW		DC.B 3			; length			DC.B $09		; Control-I			DC.B 'R'		; Reset firmware			DC.B $0D		; carriage return		ENDP***************************************************************** DevStatus** Another highly functional call.* ***************************************************************		EXPORT	DevStatus      DevStatus      PROC               jsr IsItSafe                jmp Exit4		ENDP***************************************************************** DevAsyncRead**   CompletionRoutine   LONG*   DataLength          WORD*   PtrToBuffer         LONG**   output:*   actual length read	WORD* Another really useful routine!* ***************************************************************		EXPORT	DevAsyncRead   DevAsyncRead   PROC               DefineStackAsyncRead_rtl1 block 3AsyncRead_rtl2 block 3ReadBuffer     long 0ReadLength     word 0ReadComplete   long 0ActualLength	word 0               jsr IsItSafe               bcc Yes                jmp Exit10Yes	; 			   lda #0			   sta actualLength,s			                  jmp Exit10			   		ENDP***************************************************************** DevWriteBack**      Completion routine ptr   LONG*      BufferSize      			WORD*      BufferAddress   			LONG****************************************************************		EXPORT	DevWriteBack    DevWriteBack    PROC               jsr IsItSafe               jmp Exit10		ENDP***************************************************************** DevIsItSafe**    Output:  Safety    WORD    boolean** * EntryPoint to driver from outside.** Safety is true if it is safe, false if not.* ***************************************************************		EXPORT	DevIsItSafe    DevIsItSafe    PROC               DefineStack RTL1           block 3RTL2           block 3Result         word                jsr IsItSafe               bcc Yes               lda #False               sta Result,sGetOut         lda #0               jmp Exit0Yes            lda #True                sta Result,s               bra GetOut		ENDP***************************************************************** IsItSafe** Common routine to see if the device we want to deal with* is switched in.** If it is safe, a-reg is xet to zero and carry is clear.* If it is NOT safe, a-reg is set to error code and carry is*    set. * ***************************************************************		EXPORT	IsItSafe       IsItSafe       PROC				lda >$E0C02D            ; Read slot state.				and #$0002           	; bit 1 set means external				bne NotOn 				pha						; it's internal, so find out if it's				pha						; AppleTalk or serial firmware				pha				pha						; 4 word spaces for result				pha						; A reg value, don't care				pha						; x reg value, don't care				pha						; y reg value, don't care				lda #$FE1F				; the entry point to a routine which				pha						; returns system information				_FWEntry				pla						; Y register has ROM version				plx						; get unused values off stack				plx				plx					and #$00FF				; in bits 7 - 0				cmp #3					; Version 3 or greater has AppleTalk				blt ExitSafe			; in slots 1 or 2 				lda >$E101C0			; Read AppleTalk port location				and #$00FF				; lo byte only				cmp #1					; AppleTalk is in Slot 1				bne ExitSafe NotOn			lda #PortNotOn          ; set error to port not turned on				bra ExitNotSafeExitSafe 				lda #0					; no problemsExitNotSafe		cmp #1				rts		ENDP****************************************************************** PortAlert** Alert box to tell user that the appropriate port is not turned* on.** no parameters on stack*****************************************************************		EXPORT	PortAlert      PortAlert      PROC                _InitCursor              ; restore cursor back to arrow               pha                      ; make room for result               _GetMasterSCB               pla               pha                      ; make room for result of alert call                and #$80                 ; check mode                beq mode320              ; 320 mode               pushlong #alerttemp640   ; use 640 mode template               bra GoOnmode320        pushlong #alerttemp320   ; use 320 mode templateGoOn           pushlong #$0000               _StopAlert;              jsr WaitCursor           ; set to watch again                pla                      ; get the item hit off stack               rts		ENDP  ;                Copy DynamicExits		EXPORT	DynamicExits    DynamicExits    PROC* in a Dynamic exit we need to save 2 RTLs		EXPORT	exit20exit20		;		               tax               lda  5,s               sta  25,s               lda  3,s               sta  23,s               lda  1,s               sta  21,s               tsc               clc               adc  #20               tcs               txa               brl  exit0		EXPORT	Exit16Exit16		;		               tax               lda  5,s               sta  21,s               lda  3,s               sta  19,s               lda  1,s               sta  17,s               tsc               clc               adc  #16               tcs               txa               brl  Exit0		EXPORT	Exit14Exit14		;		               tax               lda  5,s               sta  19,s               lda  3,s               sta  17,s               lda  1,s               sta  15,s               tsc               clc               adc  #14               tcs               txa               brl  Exit0		EXPORT	Exit12Exit12		;		               tax               lda  5,s               sta  17,s               lda  3,s               sta  15,s               lda  1,s               sta  13,s               tsc               clc               adc  #12               tcs               txa               bra  Exit0		EXPORT	Exit10Exit10		;		               tax               lda  5,s               sta  15,s               lda  3,s               sta  13,s               lda  1,s               sta  11,s               tsc               clc               adc  #10               tcs               txa               brl  Exit0		EXPORT	Exit8Exit8		;		               tax                      ; Standard 8 bytes input exit               lda  5,s               sta 	13,s               lda  3,s               sta  11,s               lda  1,s               sta  9,s               pla               pla               pla               pla               txa               brl  Exit0		EXPORT	Exit6Exit6		;		               tax                      ; Standard 6 bytes input exit               lda  5,s               sta  11,s               lda  3,s               sta  9,s               lda  1,s               sta  7,s               pla               pla               pla               txa               brl  Exit0		EXPORT	Exit4Exit4		;		               tax                      ; Standard 4 bytes input exit               lda  5,s               sta  9,s               lda  3,s               sta  7,s               lda  1,s               sta  5,s               pla               pla               txa               brl  Exit0		EXPORT	Exit2Exit2		;		               tax                      ; Standard 2 bytes input exit               lda  5,s               sta  7,s               lda  3,s               sta  5,s               lda  1,s               sta  3,s               pla               txa		EXPORT	Exit0Exit0		;		               cmp  #1               	; Standard 0 byte input exit               rtl		ENDP		END